    "result_text": "Full suite green: **283 tests, 0 failures**.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the rule that rejects creating an owner when the owner's city already contains 8 owners, returning HTTP 400.\n\nChanges:\n\n1. **`CityOwnerLimitExceededException.java`** (new) \u2014 a `RuntimeException` mirroring the existing `DailyOwnerRegistrationLimitExceededException`, thrown when the per-city cap is reached.\n\n2. **`ClinicServiceImpl.java`** \u2014 in `saveOwner`, added a `hasReachedCityLimit(owner)` check (after the daily-cap check, before city resolution) that throws the new exception. The helper counts existing owners whose city matches the new owner's city (using the existing `normalize` helper, so casing/whitespace differences are treated as the same city) and rejects at a `MAX_OWNERS_PER_CITY = 8` threshold. A `null` city is not subject to the cap.\n\n3. **`ExceptionControllerAdvice.java`** \u2014 added an `@ExceptionHandler` for `CityOwnerLimitExceededException` that maps it to a `400 Bad Request` `ProblemDetail`, consistent with the daily-limit handler.\n\nThe pre-existing `Cp14Tests` acceptance test (which expects the 9th owner in a city to be rejected with 400) passes, `Cp13Tests` (daily cap with distinct cities) still passes, and the full suite is green.",
